                    <!-- Step-by-Step Derivation Proof -->
                    <div class="derivation-box p-5 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/80 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-neb-600 space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-base">NEB Exam Standard Proof:</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm">From the similarity of triangles:</p>
                        <div class="text-center font-mono text-sm">
                            $$\frac{|\Delta \vec{v}|}{v} = \frac{\Delta s}{r} \implies |\Delta \vec{v}| = \frac{v}{r} \Delta s$$
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-sm">Dividing both sides by $\Delta t$:</p>
                        <div class="text-center font-mono text-sm">
                            $$\frac{|\Delta \vec{v}|}{\Delta t} = \frac{v}{r} \left(\frac{\Delta s}{\Delta t}\right)$$
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-sm">Taking the limit as $\Delta t \to 0$:</p>
                        <div class="text-center font-mono text-sm">
                            $$a_c = \lim_{\Delta t \to 0} \frac{|\Delta \vec{v}|}{\Delta t} = \frac{v}{r} \left(\lim_{\Delta t \to 0} \frac{\Delta s}{\Delta t}\right) = \frac{v}{r} \cdot v$$
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-neb-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-neb-900 dark:text-neb-200 font-bold text-center py-3 rounded-lg text-sm sm:text-base">
                            $$a_c = \frac{v^2}{r} = \omega^2 r = v\omega$$
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">
                            <strong>Direction:</strong> As $\Delta t \to 0$, angle $\Delta \theta \to 0$, placing $\Delta \vec{v}$ perpendicular to velocity $\vec{v}$ and pointing directly towards center $O$.
                        </p>
                    </div>
