                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <!-- Problem 1 -->
                    <div class="p-5 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 space-y-3">
                        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                            <span class="bg-neb-100 text-neb-800 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-neb-300 text-xs font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded">NEB 2078 Model Question</span>
                            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">4 Marks</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm sm:text-base">
                            <strong>Q1:</strong> A car of mass $1000\text{ kg}$ negotiates a curved banked road of radius $50\text{ m}$ at an angle of $15^\circ$. If the coefficient of static friction between tires and road is $0.2$, calculate the maximum safe speed of the car. [Take $g = 9.8\text{ m/s}^2$]
                        </p>
                        <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-emerald-500 space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 font-mono">
                            <p><strong>Given:</strong> $m = 1000\text{ kg}$, $r = 50\text{ m}$, $\theta = 15^\circ$, $\mu = 0.2$, $g = 9.8\text{ m/s}^2$</p>
                            <p><strong>Formula:</strong> $v_{\text{max}} = \sqrt{r g \left( \frac{\mu + \tan\theta}{1 - \mu \tan\theta} \right)}$</p>
                            <p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>
                            <p>$\tan(15^\circ) \approx 0.2679$</p>
                            <p>$\mu + \tan\theta = 0.2 + 0.2679 = 0.4679$</p>
                            <p>$1 - \mu \tan\theta = 1 - (0.2 \times 0.2679) = 1 - 0.05358 = 0.9464$</p>
                            <p>$v_{\text{max}} = \sqrt{50 \times 9.8 \times \left( \frac{0.4679}{0.9464} \right)} = \sqrt{490 \times 0.4944} = \sqrt{242.25} \approx \mathbf{15.56\text{ m/s}}$</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">Answer: Maximum safe speed = 15.56 m/s (or 56.02 km/h)</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Problem 2 -->
                    <div class="p-5 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 space-y-3">
                        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                            <span class="bg-neb-100 text-neb-800 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-neb-300 text-xs font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded">NEB Board Standard</span>
                            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">4 Marks</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm sm:text-base">
                            <strong>Q2:</strong> A stone of mass $0.5\text{ kg}$ is tied to a string $1\text{ m}$ long and whirled in a vertical circle. If the tension at the lowest point is $25\text{ N}$, find the velocity of the stone at the lowest and highest points. [Take $g = 9.8\text{ m/s}^2$]
                        </p>
                        <div class="pl-4 border-l-2 border-emerald-500 space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 font-mono">
                            <p><strong>Given:</strong> $m = 0.5\text{ kg}$, $r = 1\text{ m}$, $T_L = 25\text{ N}$, $g = 9.8\text{ m/s}^2$</p>
                            <p><strong>Formula at Lowest Point:</strong> $T_L - mg = \frac{m v_L^2}{r} \implies v_L = \sqrt{\frac{r(T_L - mg)}{m}}$</p>
                            <p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>
                            <p>$mg = 0.5 \times 9.8 = 4.9\text{ N}$</p>
                            <p>$v_L = \sqrt{\frac{1 \times (25 - 4.9)}{0.5}} = \sqrt{\frac{20.1}{0.5}} = \sqrt{40.2} \approx \mathbf{6.34\text{ m/s}}$</p>
                            <p><strong>At Highest Point (Energy Conservation):</strong></p>
                            <p>$v_T^2 = v_L^2 - 4gr = 40.2 - 4(9.8)(1) = 40.2 - 39.2 = 1.0\text{ m}^2/\text{s}^2$</p>
                            <p>$v_T = \sqrt{1.0} = \mathbf{1.0\text{ m/s}}$</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">Answer: Velocity at lowest point = 6.34 m/s; Velocity at highest point = 1.00 m/s</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
