                            On an unbanked road, required centripetal force depends entirely on friction between tire and road, which is unreliable (especially when wet/icy) and causes severe tire wear. Banking inclines the road, allowing a component of normal reaction ($N \sin\theta$) to safely provide centripetal force without depending on friction.
