                            <strong>No, work done is zero.</strong> Work $W = \vec{F} \cdot \vec{s} = F s \cos\theta$. Since centripetal force is always directed radially inward toward the center and instantaneous displacement is along the tangent, the angle $\theta = 90^\circ$. Because $\cos 90^\circ = 0$, work done by centripetal force is identically zero.
